  "hypothesis": "Event preparation evaluates rounded endpoint coordinates for every overlappingY edge pair,including many pairs whose computedX hulls are strictly disjoint. Precompute conservative hulls once per edge,then reject certified separated pairs before division. This removes repeated endpoint work rather than widening its SIMD. Extra range preparation,branches,allocated capacity and admitted peak may offset savings. Revision:actual XRE1101 codegen shows a232B out-of-line Create call in the per-edge preparation loop,which already loaded Y bounds. Force-inline this functional builder so those values/address checks can be shared;the range algorithm and storage are otherwise identical. No saving is presumed.",
  "intendedEndState": "One temporary EdgeRange workspace sized to maximum shape count,reused across non-overlapping shape preparations. Reserve before allocation and release after actual users finish on success/failure. Retained raster fields,edge56B representation and Band/draw bodies remain unchanged. Nonfinite/degenerate edges get unbounded hulls and preserve original path. No cache,pool,parser/layout policy or public API.",
  "mathematicalProof": "XEB1100 validates the monotonic-rounding certificate on actual Edge operations. For finite originalY/nonzero finite rounded deltaY and finite originX/deltaX,the rounded fraction is0..1 and computedX lies between originX and rounded(originX+deltaX). Strictly disjoint hulls cannot make original endpoint differences opposite in sign,so no original intersection event can be omitted. Do not substitute original endpointX. All pair polls occur before the new exclusion. For other pairs every bound,endpoint/subtraction/intersection operation and event order is verbatim. Reversing five substitutions reconstructs the whole original production source;Band/draw source is explicitly identical.",
